---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SidebandDemo from '../components/demos/SidebandDemo.astro';
import { settings } from '../lib/site';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return settings.showDemos ? [{ params: { demos: 'demos' } }] : [];
}
---

<BaseLayout title="Demos" description="Interactive demo: estimating a background from sidebands and extracting a small signal, as done in particle-physics analyses.">
  <header class="page-head blueprint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Demos</p>
      <h1>Signal from noise, interactively</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A toy version of a technique I use every day: estimate the background under a peak from the regions beside it,
        subtract it, and check how well the true signal is recovered.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <div class="wrap content">
    <section aria-labelledby="sideband-title">
      <h2 id="sideband-title">Sideband subtraction</h2>
      <p>
        A Λ hyperon decays into a proton and a pion. Combining every proton with every pion gives a mass spectrum in
        which real Λs pile up in a narrow peak, on top of a smooth background of random pairings. The background under
        the peak cannot be measured directly, so it is estimated from two <em>sidebands</em> on either side and
        subtracted.
      </p>
      <p>
        Move the sliders: with less signal, more background or worse detector resolution the estimate gets noisier
        and the significance (S/√B) drops. The same reasoning applies to any measurement where a weak signal sits on a
        background, from sensor data to quality control.
      </p>
      <SidebandDemo fig="D1" />
      <p class="note">
        Simulated data only; the numbers are illustrative and are not results from any experiment.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .content {
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    max-width: calc(52rem + 2 * var(--gutter));
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }
  p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .note {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
